      "text": "To convert from spherical coordinates $(\\rho,\\theta,\\phi)$ to rectangular coordinates $(x,y,z)$, we can use the following formulas:\n\n\\[ x = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta \\]\n\\[ y = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta \\]\n\\[ z = \\rho \\cos \\phi \\]\n\nWith these formulas, our spherical coordinates $(\\rho, \\theta, \\phi)$ will be $(3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0)$. Plug these values into the equations and you'll get your rectangular coordinates:\n\n\\[ x = 3 \\cdot \\sin 0 \\cdot \\cos 0 \\]\n\\[ y = 3 \\cdot \\sin 0 \\cdot \\sin 0 \\]\n\\[ z = 3 \\cdot \\cos 0 \\]\n\nUsing the value of $\\sin 0 = 0$, $\\sin^2 0 = 0$, and $\\cos 0 = 1$, our equations become:\n\n\\[ x = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot 1 \\]\n\\[ y = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot 1 \\]\n\\[ z = 3 \\cdot 1 \\]\n\nEvaluating each equation, we find:\n\n\\[ x = 0 \\]\n\\[ y = 0 \\]\n\\[ z = 3 \\]\n\nThus, the rectangular coordinates of the point are \\(\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}\\).",
